    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d563">

                <pb facs="0616" n="566" sameAs="frus:frus1894/pg566"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Carlos Ezeta to Mr. Gresham.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Panama</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1894-06-15"><hi rendition="#italic">June 15,
                        1894</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>I implore your Government not to deliver my brother, Antonio, to the rebels of
                    Salvador, who are only interested in assassinating him. Whatever promises they
                    make I assure you they will kill him; all are personal enemies. In 1890 Ezeta
                    conquered, captured them, and spared their lives. My brother could have taken
                    another steamer, but believed he would have more protection under the starry
                    flag of the great Republic. Is it possible that this is not so? Please
                    reply.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
